In <1317@rlgvax.UUCP> jcj@rlgvax.UUCP (Jeff Jones) writes:

>I've got a problem getting NetHack 3.0pl9 to compile correctly on a 386
>box running Interactive's 386/ix version 2.0.2.  It does compile, but
>after I install and try to run it, not matter what terminal I use 
>(including the console) I get the message "Terminal must backspace"
>and NetHack exits.  I've looked at the code where this message is,

Yes, I had this problem too. It is solved by un-commenting line 47:

#define TERMINFO	/* uses terminfo rather than termcap */
			/* should be defined for HPUX and most, but not all,
			   SYSV */

in the file include/config.h. Then recompile the whole thing, and you
should be going.

Happy hacking.

